  "body": "From https://html.spec.whatwg.org/dev/interaction.html#autocapitalization\r\n\r\n> The autocapitalize attribute never causes autocapitalization to be enabled for input elements whose type attribute is in one of the URL, E-mail, or Password states.\r\n\r\n`inputmode` attirubute has url and email, so why doesn't this consider inputmode too? we should change to \"for input elements whose type attribute is one of the URL, E-mail, or Password states, and **inputmode attiribute is one of url and email**\"",
